# These fixtures are meant to be committed, and they have to be compressed:
# the point of them is to be real gzip, bzip2, xz and zstd streams produced by
# the reference tools.
#
# A global ignore of "*.gz" is a common default (git's own sample templates
# suggest it, on the reasoning that you should commit sources rather than
# archives). That rule silently dropped all nine .gz fixtures from the first
# commit here, and nothing caught it locally because the files were still on
# disk and the tests passed. A repository .gitignore takes precedence over the
# user's global one, so re-include them explicitly.
!*.gz
!*.bz2
!*.xz
!*.zst
!*.zstd
